  // ── Wave 9. mordhau/theisle/stationeers/eco/empyrion made orderable
  //    2026-08-31 (prisma/seed-wave9-games.ts). All five have real, currently-
  //    shipping dedicated server support confirmed against SteamDB/official
  //    docs — see that file's header comment for App IDs and Docker images. ──
  mordhau: { name: "Mordhau", glyph: "⚔️" },
  theisle: { name: "The Isle", glyph: "🦕" },
  stationeers: { name: "Stationeers", glyph: "🛰️" },
  eco: { name: "Eco", glyph: "🌍" },
  empyrion: { name: "Empyrion: Galactic Survival", glyph: "🚀" },
  // ── Specialty/community family, added 2026-08-31 — deliberately NOT part of
  //    the flagship carousel (app/(marketing)/game-servers/page.tsx explicitly
  //    excludes it from the `games`/showcaseGames computation; it gets its own
  //    "Specialty & community servers" section + dedicated landing page
  //    instead). Plutonium is an open-source, community-run client/server
  //    project that lets owners of old, no-longer-monetized Call of Duty
  //    titles run private dedicated servers; Nxeon hosts the infrastructure +
  //    the open-source Plutonium tooling only — see prisma/seed-plutonium.ts
  //    for the full research/citations and the safety framing this whole
  //    family follows. "T4" is Plutonium's own internal codename for World at
  //    War (its most-documented/most-hosted title per forum.plutonium.pw and
  //    the community Docker images researched for this family). Never call
  //    this "Call of Duty hosting" anywhere — see that seed file's header. ──
  plutoniumt4: { name: "Plutonium T4 (WaW)", glyph: "🛰️" },
  // T5/T6/IW5 added 2026-08-31 alongside T4 — see prisma/seed-plutonium.ts's
  // header for the full research and safety rules shared by this whole family.
  plutoniumt5: { name: "Plutonium T5 (BO1)", glyph: "🛰️" },
  plutoniumt6: { name: "Plutonium T6 (BO2)", glyph: "🛰️" },
  plutoniumiw5: { name: "Plutonium IW5 (MW3)", glyph: "🛰️" },
